# Citation metadata for IQ-TREE3-GPU (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# GitHub renders this as the "Cite this repository" button. Validate with: cffconvert --validate
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use IQ-TREE3-GPU, please cite this work (see preferred-citation) together with the
  IQ-TREE 3 article it builds on (Wong et al. 2026, doi:10.1093/molbev/msag117), listed under
  references. A preprint DOI and a Zenodo DOI for the archived record will be added here when
  they are minted.
title: "IQ-TREE3-GPU: GPU-accelerated maximum-likelihood phylogenetic tree inference for complex amino acid substitution models"
abstract: >-
  Maximum-likelihood (ML) phylogenetic inference spends much of its computational time evaluating
  likelihoods via the Felsenstein pruning algorithm. Although previous studies have explored GPU
  acceleration of these calculations, such efforts have not translated into widely accessible,
  general-purpose tools that researchers can readily incorporate into existing phylogenetic
  workflows and computational pipelines. We introduce IQ-TREE3-GPU, which offloads the IQ-TREE 3
  likelihood kernel to GPUs while leaving the surrounding inference workflow unchanged. We
  benchmarked the implementation primarily on genome-scale amino-acid alignments constructed from
  publicly available bacterial metagenome-assembled genomes (MAGs), with complementary nucleotide
  alignment datasets extending the analysis to substantially larger computational workloads.
  Inferred topologies were identical across 182 paired CPU based IQ-TREE3 and IQ-TREE3-GPU runs
  spanning these workloads. For amino-acid phylogenetic inference with ModelFinder, IQ-TREE3-GPU
  achieved a median 3.73-fold speedup relative to CPU-only IQ-TREE 3 when both used 20 CPU
  threads, and a 34.2-fold speedup with a single CPU thread. Fixed-model nucleotide analyses
  yielded a median 0.80-fold speedup at 20 threads, with GPU acceleration becoming advantageous at
  a much higher tree complexity than in the amino-acid workflow. These results establish
  IQ-TREE3-GPU as a practical, reusable tool for accelerating computationally intensive amino-acid
  phylogenetic reconstruction within existing research workflows.
